#subtitle: Issues of taxation, budget, debt and tariffs.

= Fiscal Policy

Now that we control the Ministry of Hacienda, we are in charge of the Republic's public treasury. We can modify taxes, adjust tariffs and manage the state's debt.


@fiscal_menu

Upper-income tax rates: [+ upper_tax_rates : taxation +]

Lower-income tax rates: [+ lower_tax_rates : taxation +]

- @raise_rich: Increase taxes on the rich.
- @raise_poor
- @raise_overall: Increase overall taxes.
- @cut_rich
- @cut_poor
- @cut_overall: Cut overall taxes.
- @raise_progressive: Make the tax system more progressive by raising taxes on the rich and cutting them for the poor.
- @regressive: Shift tax weight to indirect consumption taxes easing the charge on the rich and affecting more directly to the working class.
- @tariffs: Adjust trade tariffs and custom payments.
- @debts: Manage state debt and foreign commitments.
- @root: Do not change the tax system.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@raise_rich
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; workers_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); middle_psoe -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction; coalition_dissent += 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 5; budget += 2; prr_relation -= 4; unemployed += 1; finance_goal_completed += 1; inflation -= 0.6; economic_growth -= 0.4; middle_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; caballeristas_dissent -= 3; besteiristas_dissent -= 3

Raising taxes on the rich is popular among our base, but it alienates the bourgeoisie. Increasing taxes also decreases economic demand, which may lead to more unemployment.


@raise_poor
title: Raise consumption taxes, which disproportionately affect the poor.
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 2; workers_psoe -= 4; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_psoe -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; besteiristas_dissent += 3; caballeristas_dissent += 3; workers_ap += 2; workers_pce += 2;

We have raised taxes for the poor and working class. This hurts our support among the workers.


@raise_overall
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; middle_psoe -= 4; workers_psoe -= 4; unemployed += 2; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 2; workers_psoe -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; middle_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

Raising taxes hurts our support among all those who pay taxes. [? if in_republican_socialist_conjunction : However, our coalition partners are more supportive of the idea of "shared sacrifice" than simply taxing the rich. ?] Increasing taxes also decreases economic demand, which may lead to more unemployment.


@cut_rich
title: Cut income taxes for the rich.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; upper_tax_rates -= 1; nmiddle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); prr_relation += 4*(1-dissent); dlr_relation += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.7 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 0.3; economic_growth += 0.4; caballeristas_dissent += 3; besteiristas_dissent += 3

We have reduced income and property taxes for the rich and middle class. The conservative parties approve of this orthodox economic course.


@cut_poor
title: Cut consumption taxes for the poor.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; lower_tax_rates -= 1; workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.7 if unemployed >= 5; inflation += 0.4; economic_growth += 0.4; finance_goal_completed += 1; besteiristas_dissent -= 3; caballeristas_dissent -= 3;

Our tax cuts disproportionately benefit the poor and working class.


@cut_overall
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); prr_relation += 5*(1-dissent); dlr_relation += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 1.5 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 1; economic_growth += 0.6;

Cutting taxes benefits most the rich and middle-class, who pay more taxes than the working class. Our coalition partners are happy anyway.


@raise_progressive
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if lower_tax_rates < -5 : Lower-class tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if upper_tax_rates > 5 : Upper-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates >= -5 and upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: workers_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); middle_psoe -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction; prr_relation -= 4; finance_goal_completed += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; middle_psoe -= 4 if upper_tax_rates > 1

Making the tax system more progressive is popular among our base, [? if in_republican_socialist_conjunction : but it upsets our conservative coalition partners, as well as our minimal number of bourgeois voters ?].


@regressive
title: Lower taxes on the rich, while increasing consumption taxes (which affect the working class more).
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 : Rich tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if lower_tax_rates > 5 : Lower-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: workers_psoe -= 6; middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); prr_relation += 5; dlr_relation += 4; coalition_dissent += 1; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; workers_psoe -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; besteiristas_dissent += 5; caballeristas_dissent += 5

Our regressive taxation policy benefits the rich while hurting the poor and working-class. Our conservative coalition partners approve of this orthodox economic course but our leftist allies and members disapprove it.



@tariffs
title: Change tariffs instead.

Tariffs, or taxes on international imports, are another way to finance our government.

Historically, socialists have been in favor of free trade and a low-tariff regime. Workers in export-oriented industries benefit from free trade, and they also benefit from lower prices for imported necessities. Do the present economic circumstances change these calculations?

Current tariff level: [+ tariffs : taxation +]

- @raise_tariffs
- @lower_tariffs
- @fiscal_menu: Change domestic taxes instead of tariffs.
- @root: Do not change tariffs or taxes.
- @easy_discard

@raise_tariffs
title: Raise tariffs on imports.
subtitle: +2 budget. Other countries will retaliate by increasing tariffs of their own. [? if tariffs > 5 : Further increases in tariffs will not raise revenue, as we have already nearly reached econonmic autarky. ?]
choose-if: tariffs <= 5
on-arrival: tariffs += 1; inflation += 1 if inflation > 0; inflation += 0.5 if inflation <= 0; unemployed += 1.5; budget += 2; workers_psoe -= 5; unemployed_psoe -= 5; west_relation -= 1; economic_growth -= 0.4; capital_strike_progress += 1 if tariffs >= 3

Increasing tariffs leads to higher prices for basic goods, increasing inflation and hurting consumption among the working class. Retaliatory tariffs reduce the competitiveness of Spanish exports, raising unemployment among workers. They also lead to an atmosphere of international suspicion, reducing our ability to negotiate with other countries.

On the other hand, large agricultural producers and some small businesses benefit from higher tariffs and formerly uncompetitive businesses are now able to function.

@lower_tariffs
title: Lower tariffs on imports.
choose-if: budget >= 2 and tariffs > -5
subtitle: -2 budget. [? if tariffs <= -5 : There are no tariffs left to cut. ?]
on-arrival: tariffs -= 1; budget -= 2; inflation -= 0.5; workers_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); rural_psoe += 5 if peseta_status == "devalued"; smallholders_psoe += 3 if peseta_status == "devalued"; west_relation += 1; economic_growth += 0.4; economic_growth += 0.1 if peseta_status == "devalued";

Lowering tariffs helps workers and the urban poor by reducing prices for basic necessities. In addition, other countries are pleased by lower tariffs, and are more willing to negotiate on many issues.

Cheap imports are detrimental for small-scale industries aimed at the domestic market. [? if peseta_status == "devalued" : Our agricultural sector benefits from having a devalued coin and the lower external tariffs increasing their exports ?]

@debts
title: Manage national debt.

The Republic faces significant internal debt left behind by the Primo de Rivera dictatorship, along with pressure on the peseta. However, we possess substantial gold reserves in the Banco de España.

- @repay_debt: Pay off domestic treasury bonds to restore credit confidence.
- @issue_debt: Issue new public debt bonds.
- @replenish_gold_reserves: Re-buy gold to fill the Banco de España's reserves.
- @fiscal_menu: Return to tax menu.
- @root: Do not change financial strategy.

@repay_debt
title: Repay domestic treasury bonds (-1 budget).
subtitle: -1 Budget. Improves credit rating and lowers financial panic.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and public_debt >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : We need at least +1 Budget to amortize domestic debt. ?] [? if public_debt < 1 : We don't have any more debt to pay. ?] 
on-arrival: budget -= 1; public_debt -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1; prr_relation += 2;

Paying off internal debt reassures domestic banking institutions, reduces capital flight and stabilizes public financial standing.

@issue_debt
title: Issue Public Debt Treasury Bonds (+1 Budget)
subtitle: [? if gold_reserves > 0 : Backed by Bank of Spain gold reserves. Low inflation risk. ?] [? if gold_reserves <= 0 : UNBACKED DEBT! The markets won't take it kindly, we can expect high inflation and economic penalties. ?]
choose-if: public_debt <= 9
unavailable-subtitle: We have too much debt, new bonds are practically worthless. 
on-arrival: budget += 1; public_debt += 1; gold_reserves -= 1 if gold_reserves >= 1; capital_strike_progress += 0.5 if gold_reserves >= 1; inflation += 0.6 if gold_reserves <= 0; economic_growth -= 0.3 if gold_reserves <= 0; capital_strike_progress += 2 if gold_reserves <= 0;

[? if gold_reserves > 0 : We issue new state bonds backed by our gold reserves. The funds allow us to maintain state spending and public works without unsettling the markets. ?][? if gold_reserves <= 0 : With our gold reserves depleted, issuing unbacked debt causes financial alarm. The peseta loses credibility, inflation spikes and private investors lose confidence in the <span style="color: #E3000F;">RE</span><span style="color: #D5AC27;">PUB</span><span style="color: #8845ba;">LIC</span>'s solvency. ?]
@replenish_gold_reserves
title: Issue Public Debt Treasury Bonds (-2 Budget)
subtitle: [? if gold_reserves > 0 : Backed by the Banco de España's gold reserves. Low inflation risk. ?] [? if gold_reserves <= 0 : UNBACKED DEBT! The markets won't take it kindly, we can expect high inflation and economic penalties. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least +2 Budget to replenish our gold reserves.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; gold_reserves += 1; capital_strike_progress -= 2; inflation -= 0.3;

Re-buying gold to replenish the Banco de España's treasury will reassure our domestic banking institutions, reduce capital flight and stabilize our public financial standing.
